#InPhotos | CJP protest in Delhi : Jantar Mantar sees better turnout than last time, protestors wait for Dipke

Track LIVE updates

@abhijeet_dipke @Cockroachisback https://t.co/lwLamcTO9A

The CJP protest at Jantar Mantar today had almost the same number of protestors. But the stage was bigger, the protest was better organised, crowd management was better, and there was free water and other arrangements.

The question arises again: who is paying for all this extravagance?

A few days ago, Rahul Gandhi did something similar in Kota. The stage was grand, but we know it was funded by his party, Congress.

So who is funding the CJP protest? Is it a party like AAP? Influencers like Dhruv Rathee? Some hidden figures from civil society? Who are they? Can we expect some transparency? 

@CJP_for_India 
@abhijeet_dipke

